# Standard operators that reach another standard operator by name.
#
# A name in a procedure body is resolved against the dictionary stack when
# it runs, so each pair below is a place where a program redefining the
# second name changes what the first one does. bind closes that, and the
# interpreter binds every promoted body once the whole set is promoted --
# the only moment at which a call between them can be frozen.
#
# What is left is what bind can no longer reach. bind makes what it binds
# read-only and then ignores a read-only array, so a body bound at its
# definition, before any of these names answered with an operator, keeps
# the names it had for good; the same goes for a procedure nested inside a
# body that some earlier sweep already bound. Dropping the bind from those
# definitions, and letting the promotion do it once at the right moment,
# is what empties this list.
#
# The list only shrinks. An entry that is frozen now is a failure too, so
# it cannot go stale, and a body that starts reaching a new name fails at
# once. Checked by tests/check-wrapped-bind.sh.
ashow grestore
ashow gsave
awidthshow grestore
awidthshow gsave
charpath stringwidth
composefont findresource
currenthsbcolor currentrgbcolor
eofill =
eofill pstack
erasepage grestore
erasepage gsave
erasepage setgray
execform grestore
execform gsave
execform initclip
fill =
fill pstack
findfont findfont
glyphshow grestore
glyphshow gsave
image grestore
image gsave
image setcolorspace
instroke grestore
instroke gsave
instroke infill
instroke strokepath
inueofill grestore
inueofill gsave
inueofill ineofill
inueofill uappend
inufill grestore
inufill gsave
inufill infill
inufill uappend
inustroke grestore
inustroke gsave
inustroke infill
inustroke ustrokepath
rootfont currentfont
selectfont findfont
selectfont makefont
selectfont scalefont
selectfont setfont
setcachedevice setcharwidth
setcolor currentcolorspace
sethsbcolor setrgbcolor
setpagedevice initgraphics
setpattern currentcolorspace
setpattern setcolor
setpattern setcolorspace
setuserparams setvmthreshold
shfill clip
shfill currentcolorspace
shfill fill
shfill setcolor
